# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Build output
/bin/
/dist/

# Dagger codegen artifacts are deliberately NOT ignored. `dagger.gen.go` and
# .dagger/internal/ are committed: Dagger is moving to requiring generated code
# in the tree by v1.0, and committing it now means the module builds from a
# checkout alone rather than only after somebody has run `dagger develop`. They
# are marked linguist-generated in .dagger/.gitattributes so they stay out of
# diffs and language stats. Regenerate with `dagger develop` and commit the
# result.

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Where a conformance run generates, compiles and runs a corpus entry. The
# leading underscore is what keeps it out of ./..., and so out of `go build`,
# `go vet` and the linter; a run removes its own tree, and this covers the one a
# killed run left behind. See testdata/conformance/README.md.
/internal/conformance/goadapter/_scratch/

# What `go build ./...` inside a worked conversion leaves behind. Each of those
# modules is one `package main` deliberately — a schema design is not a thing to
# import — so building one writes a binary named after its directory.
#
# The glob is over the example rather than naming one, for the reason
# example/README.md gives about everything else here: `example/` holds a tree of
# examples and adding one is adding a directory. It was `/example/parquet/parquet`
# while there was one example, and that path has not existed since the tree grew
# a level.
/example/*/parquet/parquet

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Per-issue worktrees created by the backlog loop (backlog.worktreeDir)
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-operator Claude Code settings: permissions and the unattended-run
# authorization are personal, not shared.
.claude/settings.local.json
